GRA-18 -- diffusion band mapping copied from the stale array, lagging one pass
==============================================================================
Each pass of kgraphMapDfLoop writes difntax, then swaps difntax/difotax, so after
the last pass the freshest part values are in difotax. The final copy read
difntax instead, so the mapping was always one diffusion pass behind (a one-pass
run never changed anything). bgraph_bipart_df.c reads difotax. Fix: copy difotax.

Reproducer gra18.c: kgraphMapBd(bnd=d{pass=N}) on a 2-part jagged mapping of a
24x24 grid; count vertices changed vs the initial mapping.
  cc.sh <build> GRA-18/gra18 GRA-18/gra18.c ; LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<build>/lib ./GRA-18/gra18 <N>
  pristine : pass=21->1  22->1  23->2  24->7  25->8   (lags: pass=1 never changes a vertex)
  patched  : pass=21->1  22->2  23->7  24->8  25->8   (patched[N] == pristine[N+1]; one pass recovered)
